---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Simply Plant Care handles your privacy — what we collect, what we don't, cookies, Google AdSense, and how to contact us."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="article-meta">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Simply Plant Care ("we", "us") runs the website
      simplyplantcare.com. The site is written by
      <a href="/author/zeeshan-farooq/">Zeeshan Farooq</a>, Plants
      Researcher. This page explains what information is collected when
      you use the site, and what we do with it.
    </p>
    <h2>Information we do not collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not run accounts, and we do not ask you to sign up for anything.
      We do not collect names, email addresses, or any other personal
      information through the website itself. If you email us, we receive
      whatever you include in that email, and we use it only to reply to you.
    </p>
    <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Two features on this site save information in your own browser's
      local storage, on your device only:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The <strong>Plant Care Checklist</strong> saves which tasks you have
        ticked off, so you can return later and pick up where you left off.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <strong>"Was this guide helpful?"</strong> feedback on each
        guide saves your answer for that guide, so you are not asked again.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information never leaves your device, is never sent to us, and
      you can delete it at any time by clearing your browser's site data.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site shows a small cookie consent notice when you first visit.
      If you choose Accept or Decline, we store only that choice in your
      browser's local storage, so the notice does not appear again. We set
      no tracking or advertising cookies ourselves. You can change your
      choice at any time using the "Cookie settings" link in the footer,
      which clears the stored choice and shows the notice again.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party services described below may set their own cookies when
      you use them, as described in their own policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Advertising — Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      We plan to display advertising on this site through Google AdSense.
      Google is a third-party vendor. When AdSense ads are shown:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Google uses cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this
        website or other websites.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to
        serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other
        sites on the Internet.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
        You may also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for
        personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No AdSense ads are shown on this site until AdSense is approved and
      enabled. We do not place ads on the About, Contact, Privacy Policy,
      or Terms pages. Advertising, when added, will be clearly separate
      from editorial content and will not influence what our guides
      recommend.
    </p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We do not currently run Google Analytics or any other analytics
      service on this site. If we add privacy-respecting analytics in the
      future to understand which guides are read, this policy will be
      updated before it is enabled, with the name of the service and what
      it collects.
    </p>
    <h2>Server and hosting logs</h2>
    <p>
      Like most websites, our hosting provider may keep short-term server
      logs, for example your IP address, browser type, and the pages you
      request, for security and to keep the site working. We do not use
      those logs to identify individual visitors, and we do not sell them.
    </p>
    <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Our guides may link to external reference sources, such as university
      extension services and botanical gardens, and to our Pinterest page
      at
      <a href="https://www.pinterest.com/simplyplantcare/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">pinterest.com/simplyplantcare</a>.
      We are not responsible for the privacy practices of other websites.
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This website is intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted here with a
      new "last updated" date.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: email
      <a href="mailto:hello@simplyplantcare.com">hello@simplyplantcare.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
